        "id": "table_of_contents-1",
        "text": "Subsecciones de: Chapter 11: Using Python for Microservices Development\nP\u00e1ginas: 414-437\n\u2022 Technical requirements  (415)\n\u2022 Introducing microservices  (415)\n\u2022 Learning best practices for microservices  (418)\n\u2022 Building microservices-based applications  (420)\n  \u2022 Learning microservice development options in Python  (420)\n  \u2022 Introducing deployment options for microservices  (421)\n  \u2022 Developing a sample microservices-based application  (423)\n\u2022 Summary  (436)\n\u2022 Questions  (436)\n\u2022 Further reading  (436)\n\u2022 Answers  (437)\n11\nUsing Python for\nMicroservices\nDevelopment\nMonolithic applications that are built as a single-tiered software have been a popular\noption for developing applications for many years. However, it is not efficient to deploy\nmonolithic applications in cloud platforms in terms of reserving and utilizing resources.\nThis is even true for the deployment of large-scale monolithic applications on physical\nmachines. The maintenance and development costs of such applications are always high.\nMulti-tier applications have solved this problem to some extent for web applications by\nbreaking the applications down into several tiers.\nTo meet dynamic resource demands and to reduce development/maintenance costs, the\nreal savior is a microservices architecture . This new architecture encourages applications\nto be built on loosely coupled services and deployed on dynamically scalable platforms\nsuch as containers. Organizations such as Amazon, Netflix, and Facebook have already\nmoved from a monolithic model to microservices-based architecture. Without this\nchange, these organizations couldn't have served a large number of clients.\n392     Using Python for Microservices Development\nWe will cover the following topics in this chapter:\n\u2022I Introducing microservices\n\u2022I Learning best practices for microservices\n\u2022I Building microservices-based applications\nAfter completing this chapter, you will learn about microservices and will be able to build\napplications based on microservices.",
